          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "книга (kníga) — \"a book\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "книга (kníga) from Proto-Slavic kŭniga. Vasmer, following Räsänen, takes it as a loan through early Turkic, Danube Bulgar küiniv, ultimately from Chinese k'üen, \"a scroll\"; Hungarian könyv, \"book\", has the same source. He finds the older Assyrian account less likely."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
