          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ручка (rúchka) — \"a pen\". Literally \"a little hand\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ручка (rúchka) is рука, \"hand\", with -ка, \"little\"; к turns to ч before it. The word means \"a little hand\", then \"a handle\", then \"a pen\", the thing you hold. Vasmer relates рука to Lithuanian rankà, \"hand\", and a Lithuanian verb for gathering."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
